WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.129 --> 00:00:01.248
- Welcome back, y'all.

00:00:01.248 --> 00:00:02.081
During the holidays,

00:00:02.081 --> 00:00:03.300
we had Danny DeVito here

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.850
promoting his animated movie "Migration."

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.020
I love him so much.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.250
And if you haven't seen it yet,

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.900
it is a great watch for the whole family.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:10.733
It's so good.

00:00:10.733 --> 00:00:11.566
The thing is, though,

00:00:11.566 --> 00:00:12.900
that Danny and I had a lot to talk about;

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:13.733
we're both talkers,

00:00:13.733 --> 00:00:16.500
so much, there was an
overflow of great content.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.300
You're welcome, America, in advance.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.760
Luckily, we have a chance to
share it right now with you.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.100
Here is our Kelly Extra with Danny DeVito,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.130
starting with maybe the
craziest audition story

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.810
I've ever heard.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.760
So I heard also, whenever
you used to audition,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.389
that you used to do crazy
things at your auditions.

00:00:31.389 --> 00:00:32.222
- [Danny] Yeah.

00:00:32.222 --> 00:00:33.055
- Well, like, what does that mean?

00:00:33.055 --> 00:00:33.888
- Well, the thing about an audition

00:00:33.888 --> 00:00:35.347
is you want to make an
impression, so yeah-

00:00:35.347 --> 00:00:36.180
- Stand out.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.013
- Yeah, you want to really stand out.

00:00:37.013 --> 00:00:38.863
- Yeah.
- And a couple of 'em, I,

00:00:38.863 --> 00:00:39.696
one was,

00:00:39.696 --> 00:00:42.448
my first one was I was
auditioning for a play

00:00:42.448 --> 00:00:45.000
that was at the public theater.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.990
And then, you know,

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:48.180
you just go to all these auditions

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.260
when you're an actor.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.890
Everybody who tries to
do this knows the drill.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.980
And you go and you wind up
meeting the casting directors

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.930
and they know you after a while

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.850
if they bring you in for many things.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:00.683
And some, you know,

00:01:00.683 --> 00:01:01.920
a lot, most of 'em, you don't get,

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:02.880
you don't get.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.740
So, but you wanna make an impression.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.330
And there was this one director

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:07.680
who was doing a play,

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.870
he was doing "Threepenny Opera," okay?

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:10.745
And it's,

00:01:10.745 --> 00:01:13.170
and I said, "Look, it's a small part.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.490
It's one monologue."

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:15.540
It's like,

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.807
you know,

00:01:16.807 --> 00:01:17.850
"Open the door."

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.350
When you open the door -

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.595
'cause I knew the casting woman -

00:01:20.595 --> 00:01:23.400
I said, "Stand back.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.870
Just stand back."

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.070
And she said, "Oh, Danny,"

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.747
you know, like, "What are you gonna do?"

00:01:27.747 --> 00:01:29.413
(people laughing) I said,
"Don't worry about it.

00:01:29.413 --> 00:01:30.246
Doesn't-"

00:01:30.246 --> 00:01:31.079
You know,

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:31.912
so she did it,

00:01:31.912 --> 00:01:33.497
and I laid down and I rolled in.

00:01:33.497 --> 00:01:35.280
(people laughing)

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.113
Right?

00:01:36.113 --> 00:01:38.760
And I was doing my monologue.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:39.593
I rolled-

00:01:39.593 --> 00:01:40.426
- While you're rolling?

00:01:40.426 --> 00:01:41.259
- Yeah.

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:42.150
I started it.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.069
By the time I got to the
middle of the audition -

00:01:45.069 --> 00:01:46.459
it was a little speech -

00:01:46.459 --> 00:01:49.110
I was actually on my back,

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:50.548
looking up at the director.

00:01:50.548 --> 00:01:52.560
(people laughing)

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.697
And he's looking down at me like,

00:01:54.697 --> 00:01:56.970
"This guy is (bleep)."

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:57.803
Yeah.
- Insane.

00:01:57.803 --> 00:01:58.890
- No, not funny.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:01:59.803
I was gonna say something else.

00:01:59.803 --> 00:02:00.636
- You were gonna say-

00:02:00.636 --> 00:02:01.469
- No, I was gonna say
something else with an F.

00:02:01.469 --> 00:02:02.460
- Yeah.
- He's insane.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.200
- Yeah.
- And,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.490
and, you know,

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:07.560
and I finished and I just kind of,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.290
and everybody was like,
you could hear a pin drop.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.007
And the guy went like this:

00:02:12.007 --> 00:02:13.048
"Thank you very much."

00:02:13.048 --> 00:02:15.210
(everyone laughing)

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.043
I didn't get the part.

00:02:16.043 --> 00:02:17.709
(people clapping)
- You waited by the phone.

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:18.798
Way to go.

00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:19.791
(Kelly clapping)

00:02:19.791 --> 00:02:22.140
I hear you also have a unique warmup

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.280
that you do, like, in theater?

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.113
- Yeah.

00:02:24.113 --> 00:02:25.829
- Like, what do you do?
- I have a trampoline.

00:02:25.829 --> 00:02:26.662
I have a great-

00:02:26.662 --> 00:02:27.495
- Like the mini trampoline?

00:02:27.495 --> 00:02:28.530
- Yeah, it's like about this size.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:29.550
- Yeah. No, I have one.
- Right?

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:30.690
A little bit lower than this.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:31.523
- Yeah.

00:02:31.523 --> 00:02:32.356
- And I put it

00:02:32.356 --> 00:02:33.390
in my dressing room.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:34.223
And before you go,

00:02:34.223 --> 00:02:35.190
you know, the whole idea

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.600
is you gotta get, you know, juiced up.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.500
You saw the show.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.550
- Yeah.
- Pretty high energy.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.383
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:39.383 --> 00:02:40.380
- And so

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.400
I need that, you know?

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.990
I need to get in there and-
- Yeah.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.520
- So, anyway,

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.353
I get in there before,

00:02:45.353 --> 00:02:47.070
you know, I come early,

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.060
get ready.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:48.990
I get disheveled.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:52.247
My hair is way, way wilder
than this in the show.

00:02:52.247 --> 00:02:53.398
(people laughing)
- Yeah.

00:02:53.398 --> 00:02:54.231
- And...

00:02:54.231 --> 00:02:55.897
(Kelly laughing)
- I love you so much.

00:02:55.897 --> 00:02:57.606
- [Danny] She can testify
to that. (Kelly clapping)

00:02:57.606 --> 00:02:58.530
And, you know,

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.910
and I get ready to go,

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:02.220
because we go right from the jump.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.113
As soon as that curtain opens,

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.920
you know, the audience
is ready, in for a ride.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.180
You gotta hang on.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.013
So we go.

00:03:10.013 --> 00:03:12.780
And so I need to get my stuff going,

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:13.620
you know, my blood
- Yeah.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.780
- and all my lymph glands,

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.903
everything shaking.
- You need to get pumped.

00:03:17.903 --> 00:03:18.736
This is your pump.

00:03:18.736 --> 00:03:19.710
- So I pump on this thing.
- Yeah.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:22.110
- I go up and down. Yeah,
I get ready on that. Yeah.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:25.710
- I cannot skip or jump on a
trampoline without smiling.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.210
- Well, it's a great thing.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.470
- I know. It makes me happy.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:29.610
- The thing I have to do, though,

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.396
is I really do have to hold on.

00:03:31.396 --> 00:03:32.850
(people laughing)

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.230
- Oh.
- I have to hold on.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.820
I'll hold onto the wall

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:36.990
or I'll hold onto, like,

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.760
there's, like, a coat hook

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.020
that's nearby

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.095
that I dread winding up on.

00:03:42.095 --> 00:03:43.535
(people laughing)

00:03:43.535 --> 00:03:45.213
But I hold onto it.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:47.813
- I'm the,

00:03:47.813 --> 00:03:48.646
I'm, like, not,

00:03:48.646 --> 00:03:49.479
I'm a bad mom.

00:03:49.479 --> 00:03:51.000
I will get on with my daughter

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.560
and be like, "Let's play Crack the Egg."

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:53.575
And I'm trying to pop her up.

00:03:53.575 --> 00:03:54.408
(people laughing)
- Oh, yeah?

00:03:54.408 --> 00:03:56.190
- And she's like, "Mom,
don't jump with me.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.023
Don't jump."

00:03:57.023 --> 00:03:58.830
I'm like, I'm trying to just make her fly.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:03:59.820
Like, yeah.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:00.935
I'm opposite.

00:04:00.935 --> 00:04:03.180
I've also been highly
injured on one before.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.080
I, like, right before -

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.040
you can edit this out -

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.900
but right before was school picture day.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:07.733
The next day.

00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:08.820
This was literally what happened.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.350
I was on my friend Lauren's trampoline

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.060
and I was trying to see
how high I could get,

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:12.893
and I was, like,

00:04:12.893 --> 00:04:13.742
all of a sudden I was up there

00:04:13.742 --> 00:04:14.575
and I was like, "Oh my god,
I'm as tall as this tree."

00:04:14.575 --> 00:04:15.408
And I was coming down.

00:04:15.408 --> 00:04:17.195
I was like, "I am not
over the trampoline."

00:04:17.195 --> 00:04:18.420
(people laughing)

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.550
And I racked myself

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.050
and then fell on the ground

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.916
and face-hit a fire ant pile.

00:04:23.916 --> 00:04:25.890
(audience reacting) Have
you ever had fire ant bites?

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.390
Well, it looks like acne.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:28.950
And it literally was like

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.736
I had fire ant bites
that looked like pimples.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:31.980
(audience reacting)

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:33.657
I was really cool in school.

00:04:33.657 --> 00:04:35.340
(people laughing)

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:36.173
- That is-

00:04:36.173 --> 00:04:38.338
- I was hit on an
extraordinary amount of times.

00:04:38.338 --> 00:04:40.306
(audience applauding)

00:04:40.306 --> 00:04:41.139
(audience cheering)

00:04:41.139 --> 00:04:41.972
Alright, y'all.

00:04:41.972 --> 00:04:45.457
Remember to catch Danny in
"Migration." We love you.

